{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names","id":826629,"title":"Secret identities and true names","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-09T00:30:36-08:00","id":826629,"title":"Secret identities and true names","content":"How do you separate &quot;sleeper&quot; and mage? I know mages can make up new names, but what about going to meet with your cabal mates and order? Given today's tech, and a mage's abilities, I find it hard to believe that one could keep their identities separate.<br /> <br /> Mages wouldn't have to use the info to hurt you, they could sell/trade it for resources and services. I also find it hard to believe that many mages would dress elaborately and have almost serial killer-like movement patterns for when and where they practice magic or interact with other mages (aka not doing it too close to home).<br /> <br /> A Forces mage could just see if you have a phone, and unless you are very paranoid, or taken an identity seminar ingame, they could probably know you instantly. Track records, addresses, plot a web of your contacts, scan them for info and home in on you. This isnt even taking into consideration the wealth of things information gatherers could do with the other 9 arcana, especially conjunctionally.<br /> <br /> Is it easy for your name to end up in the wrong hands in mage society? Does it usually take beginner mages a while to build solid defensive behaviors and practices? I know this is a game about the unknown and the paranoia of consequence, but I sometimes struggle to envision how information flows in this world.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that, logically, it would be very hard to keep your true name a secret unless you dedicated every aspect of yourself to it. You would need to be the kind of person that can throw away an identity and lifestyle easily. Otherwise, you need to work defense and damage control with arcana to constantly fudge your sympathy and screw around with your identity and how others perceive you. Finally, I think some people don't care if their true name is known. They either know too many important people that anything done to them would be brought into the spotlight. Additionally, they set out to know plenty of names and be known by many, so they become part of a network that almost functions like a cold war state. Nobody wants to shoot first.<br /> <br /> This still brings to mind Seers and other enemies who would either destroy you or ceaselessly tempt you with this info, but I would assume info like this isn't readily available to these enemies without due effort.<br /> <br /> Anyway, am I on the right track? Do you guys have clever methods of keeping your name hidden while still being physically present in the mage community and leading your normal life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":11166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","user":"kryptonitekrusher","date":".  Tablet typing isn't fun 02-09-2016, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T02:01:18-08:00","id":826649,"title":"","content":"In our chrnicle, I dont even care about my true identity, name, whatever. I give both names, real and shadow, I dont mind. If anyone is going to fuck me hard, he is gonna do it besides that knowledge, I think.<br /> <br /> Im a Free Council Obrimos from the Transhuman Engineers, living among enemies (the whole City Concilium hates me). I'm a PhD professor in the Barcelona University, whit lots of papers publiched in my name. Hoy could I hide my true identity form a Seer? Its just ridicolus. I imagine that the book consider that name subterfuges thinking in a &quot;global?&quot; chrnicle, not a local one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6851-sangros","name":"Sangros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6851_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T02:02:49-08:00","id":826650,"title":"","content":"It's not really that big a deal most of the time.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, the best way would probably be to take up a false identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T02:12:12-08:00","id":826652,"title":"","content":"I beleave that in modern society and in some extent the past that the secret of your true name is mostly protectedby politeness. In polite mage society you don't try to find out another mages true name because it is very impolite to do it. Sure if you have an enemy you try to find it out but for most mages you don't waste the time or resources. Besides what are you going to use the true name for? Are you constantly scrying on the 30+ mages in your consilium? When do you have time for your other projects/obsessions and your own life?<br /> <br /> Also if you are going to use arcana to find out the true name of a paranoid mage you most probably are going to trigger their unseen senses and thus their protection. If you are using mundane means you have to be better than the mage and most certainly overcome their magic as well.<br /> <br /> To summarize mages don't bother finding out other mages true names unless they have a good reason to find out and then it is possible but will likely lead to conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T02:14:42-08:00","id":826654,"title":"","content":"Yeah, most Mages establish at least one false identity on top of their Shadow Name. The Shadow Name is how you're identified magically, but the false identity is there so that if someone digs they hit that first and either buy it or their activities have alerted you to their digging and you can enact countermeasures.<br /> <br /> I know in Dave's APs true names tend to crop up eventually as a sign of trust. It's a big deal to know someone trusts you enough to give you something that could be weaponized against them and only them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-09-2016, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T03:13:25-08:00","id":826675,"title":"","content":"<b>sympathetic</b> names. Not true names.<br /> <br /> And most mages have a fake identity to pay their bills, lease their house, and suchlike. Looking at someone's driving licence is no guarantee that you just found their sympathetic name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T04:43:53-08:00","id":826699,"title":"","content":"Does the connection between an individual and their sympathetic name go both ways?<br /> I.e. could Bob the Mage go follow the link from himself to, say, his name as present on the page of a book or in another person's mind?<br /> That would allow for tricks like a Space2/Mind1/Fate1 spell to 'scry the last person who learned my name with ill intent' or maybe Space1/Mind1 to 'know the location of everyone in a radius of X who knows my sympathetic name', or an Unveiling of Mind to see the presence of your Name in the Minds of those around you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T04:47:26-08:00","id":826700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names#post826629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">have almost serial killer-like movement patterns for when and where they practice magic or interact with other mages (aka not doing it too close to home).</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, the overwhelming majority of serial killers are actually highly territorial and do kill fairly close to their home. They tend to be local rather than mobile; in fact, most have <i>jobs</i> that provide access to potential victims. Opportunity is everything to a serial killer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, now on to the actual discussion. <br /> <br /> <br /> First, I'd like to point out that sympathetic names, IIRC, are only bad (magically) if someone uses sympathetic magic (ie Space) to target you. There are spells and techniques to deal with someone targetting you with Space. At least there was in 1e, and I'm assuming a number of them are going to exist in 2e. Other uses of a sympathetic name could mean targetting your mortal family and friends. <br /> <br /> Much like Demon, Mage is a game that evokes Cold War-era paranoia. Much like the Cold War, however, there tends to be a certain polite code of conduct. The three factions of Awakened society (Assembly, Pyramid, Diamond) don't want to go to actual war, because, much like the threat of nuclear winter, that's a situation where Mutually Assured Destruction comes into play. No one wants a mage war. Very few want to escalate to harming on someone else's family, because then the same favor is payed back. <br /> <br /> So, why use Shadow Names and fake IDs at all, then? Because its always best to just remove as much temptation as possible. Its like going jogging at night in the park. Most people realize that doing that is putting yourself at risk of being attacked. Why present yourself as an easy target? Sure, if someone REALLY wanted to, that mage could find out all your names, sympathetic, fake, shadow, etc. That's not the point. The point is to make yourself less of an obvious target with a smaller window of opportunity. Casually using your sympathetic name is like waving a red flag or painting a bull's eye target on your back. Most criminals and villains are opportunistic. If they think that you're leaving them an opportunity, they'll take it. If they have to put in work, chances are they'll simply pass you by in favor of following their personal Obsessions instead. Why go around killing each other when there's so many juicy <i>mysteries </i>running around to study and gain power from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:06:50-08:00","id":826707,"title":"","content":"Remember that usually, if you are checking out the Mage, Mage can sense that. And it's hard to actually *find* mages who are not running a ton of spells on them; Mage teacher, who has no spells on him active, and is not casting magic, will look like a simple sleeper math teacher to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:22:22-08:00","id":826720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826707#post826707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that usually, if you are checking out the Mage, Mage can sense that. And it's hard to actually *find* mages who are not running a ton of spells on them; Mage teacher, who has no spells on him active, and is not casting magic, will look like a simple sleeper math teacher to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK you can look for the mana in their pattern, Prime Mage sight gives you their nature as an extra feature of that Sight, and every other Sight can tell you if someone is supernatural with 5 successes on the Occult + Int.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:30:09-08:00","id":826728,"title":"","content":"Yeah but are you going to check pattern of each single person around you? It's less about being investigation-proof, and more about not giving anyone a reason to look at you. It's kind of like how easy it would be to find each and single one of people commiting tax crimes, but we don't, because we literally can't *check every and single taxpayer*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T06:19:26-08:00","id":826760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826675#post826675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>sympathetic</b> names. Not true names.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Old habits die hard and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T06:24:51-08:00","id":826762,"title":"","content":"A lot of these assumptions seem to work only for mages who regularly socialize, and yet have no social skills whatsoever. I would say that in a Consilium, magically invading another person's phone is easily recognised and entirely unacceptable, and that whatever way there is to get around obstacles to finding information on a fellow's real life, actually pursuing that might be somewhere between highly rude and actually illegal.<br /> <br /> Mages on the same side don't need to be in a cold war state if they conduct themselves with some basic politeness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T06:30:34-08:00","id":826773,"title":"","content":"Plus another reason to maintain a shadow name is to ground out your sympathy to magic so your magic doesn't affect your loved ones via sympathy leak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T07:59:58-08:00","id":826829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826773#post826773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus another reason to maintain a shadow name is to ground out your sympathy to magic so your magic doesn't affect your loved ones via sympathy leak.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's definitely easy to forget the new Nimbus mechanics spoiled by Dave some time ago that reinforce the value of a Shadow name and persona. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:20:39-08:00","id":826915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826675#post826675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And most mages have a fake identity to pay their bills, lease their house, and suchlike. Looking at someone's driving licence is no guarantee that you just found their sympathetic name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have wondered about this. In the modern age, it is getting increasingly hard to pull this off. Sure, there are more ways to access the information needed for creating a new one with the digital age, but there are also more verification techniques and checkpoints for day to day stuff: passports and even state id's with means to connect to a database instantly to confirm the records; jobs requiring multiple forms of ID. This also assumes that you aren't trying to achieve any position of authority or reliant on higher education, such as an MD or politician, as the modern vetting process is pretty sophisticated. If a mage awakens in early adulthood or later, they would have to both rebuild a life while facing these hurdles, while also create a means to distance themselves from their existing paper trail. And this isn't even touching on the social aspect, both from having to personally withdraw from circles of those who may identify you, plus the issues of modern social media.<br /> <br /> Sure, magic can get you past these, and it isn't impossible to fabricate completely new identities through mundane means. But both require skill sets that a newly awakened mage would likely not have.<br /> <br /> I guess my question would be: how do mages create these identities? Do the Orders assist (like a magical witness protection)? Do the mages simply bite the bullet and withdraw till they can safely construct a means to hide? Do most not really bother unless they are forced to hide, due to politics/rivalries getting out of hand? Something else that I am missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:39:19-08:00","id":826931,"title":"","content":"One of great resources that Orders can use to make themselves attractive is making all the paper work for you and giving out working fake identify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:45:34-08:00","id":826936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826915#post826915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my question would be: how do mages create these identities? Do the Orders assist (like a magical witness protection)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely this one. The Order Caucuses' contacts and networks combine to sort it. Mechanically, one of the Merits you can requisition with Order Status is Alternate Identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:02:11-08:00","id":826948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826915#post826915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> verification techniques and checkpoints for day to day stuff: passports and even state id's with means to connect to a database instantly to confirm the records; jobs requiring multiple forms of ID. This also assumes that you aren't trying to achieve any position of authority or reliant on higher education, such as an MD or politician, as the modern vetting process is pretty sophisticated.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the fact that magic is extremely helpful to alter records, change appearance, and similar matters, and the Orders have likely distilled the creation of alternate identities to a Fallen science, if push come to shove, most mages also have some form of &quot;these aren't the droids you're looking for&quot; powers. Things as simple as driver's license and passport checks and most questions can be entirely avoided or the target can be made to see or hear whatever the mage wants, including everything from direct mind control to using Prime to create platonic identification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:03:58-08:00","id":826949,"title":"","content":"Quick questions: can you use a Mind spell to discover a Sleeper's Sympathetic Name? If I use Mind to discover's another Mage's Sympathetic Name, can he fight back by using the same Arcanum to erase that knowledge from my mind?<br /> <br /> I'm asking because the Mind Arcanum seems like the most direct way of discovering that kind of information. I assume the Persona Merit helps against this sort of intrusion. You could do it in other ways, though. Using Death or Spirit to ask a corresponding ephemeral being to spy on your rival Mage if he's too good with Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-09-2016, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:07:02-08:00","id":826951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826949#post826949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick questions: can you use a Mind spell to discover a Sleeper's Sympathetic Name? If I use Mind to discover's another Mage's Sympathetic Name, can he fight back by using the same Arcanum to erase that knowledge from my mind?<br /> <br /> I'm asking because the Mind Arcanum seems like the most direct way of discovering that kind of information. I assume the Persona Merit helps against this sort of intrusion. You could do it in other ways, though. Using Death or Spirit to ask a corresponding ephemeral being to spy on your rival Mage if he's too good with Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no reason any of those things wouldn't be possible. That said, using magic, let alone mind magic, against another mage without their permission is just looking for trouble. Sleepers and most supernaturals generally won't be able to tell you're doing it, but another mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 02-09-2016, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:18:38-08:00","id":826955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826915#post826915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my question would be: how do mages create these identities? Do the Orders assist (like a magical witness protection)? Do the mages simply bite the bullet and withdraw till they can safely construct a means to hide? Do most not really bother unless they are forced to hide, due to politics/rivalries getting out of hand? Something else that I am missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking it was Guardians duty, like Winter Court makes this kind of thing for changelings. But in 2ED <i>all</i> Orders are Mystery Cults networks, so they can pull their Sleeper members and say &quot;We need cover story for John - you do ID, you there make him new papers in DMV and Tom from police pull his things&quot;, I assume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-09-2016, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:24:04-08:00","id":826957,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't use Mind to find out Sympathetic Name; it doesn't feel like it falls unde Arcanum's purview. I think better fit would be Space or Prime. <br /> One of reasons why we usually use &quot;after you Awakened, you moved to a different town than your home&quot; as a standard procedure for new Chronicles is because it's much easier to start &quot;new fake life&quot; in new city, while it's also easy to maintain your old life, family, and friends; usually a Skype call or few hours of driving is enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:28:13-08:00","id":826959,"title":"","content":"Unless they've erased the knowledge of their Sympathetic Name from their own mind (Which is a possibility) I see no reason you couldn't pluck that information from their heads with Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:32:17-08:00","id":826964,"title":"","content":"I think that Prime would be useful for finding out the mage's Supernal name - the one they signed on the Watchtower. <i>Sympathetic</i> name seems to me more like a Space purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:15:38-08:00","id":827023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826936#post826936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Largely this one. The Order Caucuses' contacts and networks combine to sort it. Mechanically, one of the Merits you can requisition with Order Status is Alternate Identity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So it's norm to build a second identity around your mage self. I assume Guardians are going to have more than a handful.<br /> <br /> Acting and shapeshifting, as much a part of your new identity as you care for it to be, I presume?<br /> <br /> For some reason I feel you'll tell me it can't be commented on because it's a case-by-case thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I want to see if I'm on the right track.<br /> <br /> a) Asking for a sympathetic name is like asking someone for a credit card number or pay stub. It's not like a death sentence, but it shows poor manner and disrespect. It can damage social bonds.<br /> <br /> b) Orders can give you a new identity. It can be as elaborate and interesting as you want it to be.<br /> <br /> c) Sympathetic names can be as relevant as you want: paranoia vs. focusing on other aspects of the game/story (or maybe have it both ways).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:21:19-08:00","id":827030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826675#post826675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>sympathetic</b> names. Not true names.<br /> <br /> And most mages have a fake identity to pay their bills, lease their house, and suchlike. Looking at someone's driving licence is no guarantee that you just found their sympathetic name.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dang it. So wait, MOST mages have three identities?<br /> <br /> Their sympathetic self (before they awakened), their mage self, and a FAKE self that works paper trails?<br /> <br /> I guess it confuses me because I remember in Vampire, you are forced to abandon your previous life. In mage, that isn't the case. So why would you need another fake sleeper identity?<br /> <br /> Since you said &quot;most mages have a fake identity&quot; that leads me to think: &quot;Hi, I'm a mage. Excluding my mage identity standing before you, I also have a real identity and a fake identity.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:25:09-08:00","id":827036,"title":"","content":"You establish a fake Sleeper identity to throw off &quot;casual&quot; attempts to determine your Sympathetic identity. The shadow name is for identifying yourself to other Mages.<br /> <br /> So, when you come home and call your mom you're John. However you pay your bills as Paul in case anyone reads your mail. To all the other Mages you're Zeus because you really like lightning bolts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:32:53-08:00","id":827048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826936#post826936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Largely this one. The Order Caucuses' contacts and networks combine to sort it. Mechanically, one of the Merits you can requisition with Order Status is Alternate Identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Dave. I am running a Noir game, so it isn't as big of an issue (though still present), but it is something that came up a lot in games and I never was sure how to address. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=826948#post826948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Besides the fact that magic is extremely helpful to alter records, change appearance, and similar matters, and the Orders have likely distilled the creation of alternate identities to a Fallen science, if push come to shove, most mages also have some form of &amp;quot;these aren't the droids you're looking for&amp;quot; powers. Things as simple as driver's license and passport checks and most questions can be entirely avoided or the target can be made to see or hear whatever the mage wants, including everything from direct mind control to using Prime to create platonic identification.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the magic fixes, but they are good for more acute challenges. Creating a long term, effective identity that doesn't require constant magical intervention is more of what I was curious about. But good points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:33:04-08:00","id":827049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=827036#post827036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You establish a fake Sleeper identity to throw off &quot;casual&quot; attempts to determine your Sympathetic identity. The shadow name is for identifying yourself to other Mages.<br /> <br /> So, when you come home and call your mom you're John. However you pay your bills as Paul in case anyone reads your mail. To all the other Mages you're Zeus because you really like lightning bolts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow, that's just so weird to me. I guess it makes sense though. Now I'm trying to imagine having all correspondence come to me under a different name, yet still talking to my family and friends with my regular name.<br /> <br /> OK, making more sense now. I guess I never realized how that could go on so easily. &quot;Oh, that mail? Probably some guy that used to live here.&quot; &quot;Yeah, they think I'm a dentist office that used to go by the same number.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cool, cool, cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:42:23-08:00","id":827057,"title":"","content":"Now, if you <i>really </i>want to disappear? Become a Time Master, go back and then prevent yourself from being born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:48:21-08:00","id":827063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=827057#post827057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if you <i>really </i>want to disappear? Become a Time Master, go back and then prevent yourself from being born.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't that like an Archmastery thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T15:16:06-08:00","id":827128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=827063#post827063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Isn't that like an Archmastery thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>DaveB mentioned how Time Masters in 2e can actually travel back in time, but only as far as their own personal timeline. I guess the deciding factor is when that point of origin actually is: birth? conception? We don't know yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:57:38-08:00","id":827215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=827063#post827063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that like an Archmastery thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, as Dave mentions in your time thread you destroy your own personal past in order to travel back. That doesn't destroy you though. You could theoretically go back and kill your parents to prevent your birth and yet you wouldn't disappear. You'd have a very It's a Wonderful Life experience from it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T18:26:44-08:00","id":827236,"title":"","content":"I wonder how many Masters of Time have someone they've never met come up to them and say, &quot;So, Teacher, I fucked up...That said, I've attained Mastery in Time!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T04:13:33-08:00","id":827398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in 2ED all Orders are Mystery Cults networks, so they can pull their Sleeper members</div> </div> </div> </div> Indeed; when it comes to specialized skill sets, even if one assumes a caucus in which none of the mages have them or care to develop them, they probably have the assets to recruit somebody else that does. I'd even say it's relatively straightforward compared to something like, say, vampires, where they might feel a need to compel a bit of blood addiction or mind control to evade any of the sticking points such as not being around during the day; you use a shadow name to redirect your nimbus, and I'd say it can be relatively easy to interact with normal people with a light veneer of arcane mystery that doesn't give a lot of the weirdness away (I imagine a lot of the sleeper associates of mages assume that they're a lot less powerful than they actually are). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it confuses me because I remember in Vampire, you are forced to abandon your previous life. In mage, that isn't the case. So why would you need another fake sleeper identity?</div> </div> </div> </div> You don't have the same pressures as vampires in the sense of possibly having been found and declared dead and the whole daylight thing, but there are pressures within mage society to distance yourself from your old life just to avoid some of the complications. Indeed, I would think that more mages are troubled by their sleeper life giving away their mage one than the other way around; differences in your lifestyle as apparent to normal people create patterns that an experienced mage can see as somebody living a double life, and quite possibly a charmed one, that means they can trace a person to target, rather than interacting with a person as a mage and running their face through a search engine to find out where they live.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T04:23:39-08:00","id":827404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Become a Time Master, go back and then prevent yourself from being born</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm, if I'm reading how that magic works correctly... it might be that you don't exist as a discrete entitity walking around tangential to your own experience of the past, but go back and actually assume your life as it was at that point. So if you Unmake your entire life up until the point you were a newborn, then you'll actually be living in that newborn body, which may limit some of what you can do. I'm not sure though, there are a few details that contradict this idea, but they're currently a bit ambiguous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T04:37:38-08:00","id":827414,"title":"","content":"Now here's the question. Are all these fake IDs going to be the default that all mages start with, or is it going to be something that players are going to need to purchase through the Alternative Identity merit? Because, if its the latter? I don't feel comfortable pushing my players towards that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T04:55:29-08:00","id":827420,"title":"","content":"In 1ED I just gave it for free, and now it seems that you will be able to ask for it using Order Status like you can grab stuff using Resources. Good standing equals benefits. I like the fact that status is flexible enough that 4 dot Status person can be both official magistrate of the order, respected teacher, or HYPED NEWCOMER SUPERSTAR, or just someone who somehow gets around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T05:20:02-08:00","id":827429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=827414#post827414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now here's the question. Are all these fake IDs going to be the default that all mages start with, or is it going to be something that players are going to need to purchase through the Alternative Identity merit? Because, if its the latter? I don't feel comfortable pushing my players towards that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends if they want it to stand up to legal scrutiny or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T05:23:18-08:00","id":827431,"title":"","content":"Let's say I <i>do not</i> want it to stand up legal security - I just want new identity to rent a car for. Could I get it for free?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T07:14:02-08:00","id":827490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=827429#post827429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends if they want it to stand up to legal scrutiny or not.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would like to hear more about the default assumptions the setting makes, please. I mean, this feels like a pretty big change to me from the old game. This is beginning to feel a lot like spy territory here, and I was under the assumption that was something the Guardians and the Space Minsistry (I forget the name) invested in heavily, but not necessarily anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-10-2016, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:07:48-08:00","id":827515,"title":"","content":"Hence why it depends on how much you care if your fake id stands up to scrutiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:15:43-08:00","id":827524,"title":"","content":"Many mages don't have any kind of alternate Sleeper identity - they just take the lumps of people finding out their Sleeper name, and possibly from that their sympathetic name. That sympathetic name is not always the name on your driving licence - it's what the people with sympathetic links to a baby think of them as while their sense of self develops, so looking through someone's mortgage paperwork is not a surefire way to get it.<br /> <br /> In mage society, referring to someone by a Sleeper identity except in intimate relationships is downright rude, as rude as deadnaming someone in our world. Some Orders outright punish people who do it - and not always the ones you expect. The Arrow think it's rude and unprofessional, for example, but it's grounds for murder among Seers of the Throne, who are if anything more serious about their Shadow Names than Pentacle mages are.<br /> <br /> So, the game assumes that most mages maintain a healthy separation of their magical and mundane lives. Not having a Shadow name, or performing too much magic in your mundane persona, can screw you up. Being really invested in your Shadow persona, to the point of buying the Merit, gives Occultation-like benefits to resisting sympathetic spells when you're not &quot;in character&quot;.<br /> <br /> Some mages, though, require mortal identities that aren't their own in the course of their studies. They might have things in their pre-Awakened lives they're trying to put behind them, a need to move in radically different social circles among Sleepers, that kind of thing. For those characters, that's what the Alternate Identity Merit is for. It's a multiple-level Merit depending on how elaborate the background is. A fake ID doesn't even need the Merit, but if you're running for political office or facing federal investigation, the higher dots of it will protect your cover.<br /> <br /> Five example characters, and how they treat their lives:<br /> <br /> Herophilus never really had a choice: he was a public servant (he's a coroner) and MD before he Awakened, he's kept his old job, his Hallow's in his morgue and everyone knows it. Despite this, other mages (even Seers!) stick to calling him by his Shadow Name (or, in mixed company, &quot;Phil&quot;) rather than his real name, despite his real name being the one on his door. To do otherwise would simply be rude. Still, assuming someone wanted to do his a mischief, he's relatively vulnerable - he doesn't have the Shadow Name Merit, as he himself calls himself &quot;Phil&quot; and doesn't use the symbolism of his Shadow Name in spellcasting. He just thought it was historically appropriate when he picked it, which is fine by the Free Council's standards.<br /> <br /> Tallulah is in a position where she's losing track of her various identities and who knows her as what. She was on the run and then a sex worker before she Awakened, so was already under an assumed name. The Silver Ladder fixed her up with documentation so she could get a job in a casino (the Alternate Identity Merit, at a mid level) but she's now moving up in the world thanks to increasing Status and membership of the Sisterhood of the Blessed, to the point where the Order is having to deepen her background to fend off private investigators, represented by buying the Merit up. The rest of her cabal know the name on her mortgage, but also know the real name beneath that. Complications include the Seers knowing an earlier alias but not her current one, and the fact that she has family - it's not just her the Ladder are maintaining Alternate Identities for, it's her (Sleepwalker) sister and infant son as well.<br /> <br /> Cowl, as a Guardian, takes operational security extremely seriously. He insists on being called by his Shadow Name on business, uses different cellphones for &quot;work&quot; and &quot;Work&quot;, and takes precautions to not allow his magical work to follow him home. This is seemingly contradicted by the fact that he uses his Sleeper identity and career to run his Labyrinth, but it's a blind - the name on his business cards is <i>not</i> his real name. He actually has the maximum level of Alternate Identity, and not even the rest of the cabal know who he really is. That's how the Guardians roll.<br /> <br /> Ibn Awoke while serving in Iraq. To the Sleeper military, he left as an invalid. He doesn't have any kind of fake papers, but as he takes on undocumented work anyway, it doesn't really matter - he's taken the broad strokes of his background and uses it without the specifics like his name, lying with the truth and vanishing into the statistics. What's an enemy mage trying to find him going to do? sympathetically scry on every single homeless and minimum-wage veteran in Vegas?<br /> <br /> Tanashiriki is in a position many mages find themselves in - her Awakening Mystery Play was so traumatic it basically burned her Sleeper life down around it. She was picked up, homeless and ranting, by the Mysterium several hundred miles away from the city where she'd fled her job and immigration status while in the grip of Pandemonium. Her Order have set her up with the basics - a driving licence, a bank account for expenses - but she lives in a Sanctum and basically doesn't <i>have</i> a Sleeping identity any more. Even if someone connected the Vegas Mystagogue to the three-years-missing low-level Interpreter in New York she used to be, it wouldn't exactly help. To get her sympathetic name, you'd have to track down the correct Kenyan village. And good luck with <i>that</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 02-10-2016, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:23:38-08:00","id":827531,"title":"","content":"Reading this made me wonder something.<br /> <br /> If you had Time 5, Space 5 and a lot of spare time; how much of a Mage's identity would you need to know before you could do something like track Sisi Sole's Sympathetic Name with magic? How plausible is it to do something like &quot;Mirror Mirror on the wall, show me Sisi Sole at 1 day old&quot;? and just keep using the spell until you've got the Sympathetic name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-10-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:28:27-08:00","id":827535,"title":"","content":"Not that much, in truth. Same way that not knowing someone's sympathetic name in first ed was not actually as big a deal as people maybe more used to reading than playing would make out. It means you need a higher Potency on sympathetic spells, that's all.<br /> <br /> But there's ways to protect it with Space spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:01:24-08:00","id":827624,"title":"","content":"One thing got me curious, though. Is the &quot;reverse occultation&quot; afforded by Fame still a thing?<br /> <br /> Say your sympathetic name gets discovered and spread (a horrible scenario), are there known measures to do something about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:31:50-08:00","id":827655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=827624#post827624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing got me curious, though. Is the &quot;reverse occultation&quot; afforded by Fame still a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Occultation and Fame both mean that any Withstand level from sympathy has a minimum of your dots in the Merit, so if you have Fame 3 the withstand from sympathy can't go below 3, no matter how the link actually is.<br /> <br /> Shadow Name gives you an additional Withstand rating to spells that identify or cast on you when you're not being your mage self. <br /> <br /> So, having both Occultation 3 and Shadow Name is -4 Potency to any spells to delve into your mundane life. Annoying, but not insurmountable.<br /> <br /> As for doing something about it, depends on how advanced you or someone who owes you a favor are in the Space Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:44:17-07:00","id":1065759,"title":"","content":"I'm playing a crossover game and one beast player has invested in fame, advanced fame and alien allure atavism. In this game there's a mage with space, how should I deal with this combination? Should I combine both fame and advanced fame as Withstand against sympathy or should I only use the fame merit? And how Alien allure with expenditure satiety should play in this situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8049-53rv3r1n0","name":"53rv3r1n0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T10:08:54-07:00","id":1065835,"title":"","content":"I feel like you have Ward and Perfect Sympathy up with huge durations or you get screwed anyways. The name doesnt offer enough of a protection to warrent a huge investment protecting in this modern age.<br /> <br /> Not having the sympathetic name plus having to rely on a stick characture raises the Withstand by 4. For most things that aren't withstood, that is easily obtainable. If it is (raising the Withstand to say 7) then you can fish for the exceptional.<br /> <br /> I will say I don't think its a coincidence that sympathy can be countered by Wars (CoW to negate) *and* Perfect Sympathy (CoW to redirect) and that the first time you attempt a Mage wil Space 3 or higher now knows you tries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-21-2017, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T18:26:34-07:00","id":1145931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=827655#post827655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadow Name gives you an additional Withstand rating to spells that identify or cast on you when you're not being your mage self.<br /> <br /> So, having both Occultation 3 and Shadow Name is -4 Potency to any spells to delve into your mundane life. Annoying, but not insurmountable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, where does say that it add to the Withstand? I see:<br /> <br /> Additionally, apply dots in this Merit <b>as a </b>With-<br /> stand rating to spells that attempt to identify her or cast on her<br /> using the Sympathetic Range Attainment when in her mundane<br /> persona, to spells using the Temporal Sympathy Attainment<br /> targeting a time when she was in her mundane persona<br /> <br /> <br /> Emphasis mine, I thought the Withstand was the highest you had. So with Occultation 3, and Shadow Name 3, you get a flat 3 Withstand. Can someone point to me where does it say that both add?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T19:58:00-07:00","id":1145959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=1145931#post1145931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, where does say that it add to the Withstand? I see:<br /> <br /> Additionally, apply dots in this Merit <b>as a </b>With-<br /> stand rating to spells that attempt to identify her or cast on her<br /> using the Sympathetic Range Attainment when in her mundane<br /> persona, to spells using the Temporal Sympathy Attainment<br /> targeting a time when she was in her mundane persona<br /> <br /> <br /> Emphasis mine, I thought the Withstand was the highest you had. So with Occultation 3, and Shadow Name 3, you get a flat 3 Withstand. Can someone point to me where does it say that both add?</div> </div> </div> </div>You go with the most appropriate Withstand available, for every additional source of Withstand you add 1. So if you are being targeted by a Sympathetic Spell that's Withstood by Resolve and you have Resolve 3, Shadow Name 3, and Occultation 3, you actually have a Withstand of 5. Those aren't even the only sources of additional Withstand that could add that +1, for instance Wards and Signs from Prime 2, or Fame instead of Occultation, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T20:24:55-07:00","id":1145964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=1145959#post1145959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You go with the most appropriate Withstand available, for every additional source of Withstand you add 1. So if you are being targeted by a Sympathetic Spell that's Withstood by Resolve and you have Resolve 3, Shadow Name 3, and Occultation 3, you actually have a Withstand of 5. Those aren't even the only sources of additional Withstand that could add that +1, for instance Wards and Signs from Prime 2, or Fame instead of Occultation, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but what page indicates that you add 1 for every additional source of Withstand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T20:30:17-07:00","id":1145967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=1145964#post1145964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, but what page indicates that you add 1 for every additional source of Withstand?</div> </div> </div> </div>p114-5, &quot;Withstanding&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a spell has multiple Withstand ratings (for example, a Withstood spell cast with the Sympathetic Range Attainment) it uses the highest rating, +1 for every additional rating. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T18:33:36-07:00","id":1506686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/826629-secret-identities-and-true-names?p=1145959#post1145959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You go with the most appropriate Withstand available, for every additional source of Withstand you add 1. So if you are being targeted by a Sympathetic Spell that's Withstood by Resolve and you have Resolve 3, Shadow Name 3, and Occultation 3, you actually have a Withstand of 5. Those aren't even the only sources of additional Withstand that could add that +1, for instance Wards and Signs from Prime 2, or Fame instead of Occultation, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back from the grave. Technically Occultation isn't listed in the Merit as another source of Withstand, but I think it's a pretty worthless Merit otherwise. By the letter of the rules, your Withstand in the above example would be 4. Resolve 3 + 1 Shadow Name = 4 and your minimum Withstand would be 2 because of Occultation, but it's not relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T19:32:27-07:00","id":1506690,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">Please do not post in threads inactive for over a year. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}